
**Added after review:** a SEARCH whose `CH Q S` line would pass 510 bytes is no longer federated. With a long channel name and a long `text=`, msgq cut the line, so the responder searched for a shorter text than the user asked for and returned rows that did not match. The line is now measured as it will be sent, and a query that cannot fit is answered from this server's store only. I checked this on two linked servers with a 150-character channel and a 325-byte `text=` that the stored message does not contain: the old build returned the message, and the new one returns nothing. A short query still federates.
